retriever_type='vector' status=<RetrievalStatus.SUCCESS: 'success'> raw_results=[] processed_results=[] response_text="The notification system in HelloWorldApp implements a callback-based observer pattern using the INotifier interface as its core abstraction. The architecture operates as follows: The Manager class implements the INotifier interface and serves as the central notification hub. During initialization, the Manager instantiates Worker objects through the WorkerFactory, passing itself as the INotifier implementation via dependency injection. Each Worker maintains a reference to this INotifier instance. When workers complete their Process() methods, they invoke the Notify() method on the injected INotifier reference with completion messages. The Manager's Notify() implementation receives and logs these messages, creating a many-to-one synchronous notification pattern. This tightly-coupled design enables coordinated task completion tracking where multiple workers report back to a single manager for centralized event handling and orchestration." metadata={'query': 'How does the notification system work in the HelloWorldApp?', 'results_count': 0, 'total_results': 0, 'processing_time': 219.1298177242279, 'confidence_score': 0.95, 'has_diagram': False, 'reasoning_used': True, 'reasoning_metrics': None, 'reasoning_trace': {'original_query': 'How does the notification system work in the HelloWorldApp?', 'complexity_analysis': {'complexity_level': 'medium', 'complexity_score': 0.43999999999999995, 'complexity_factors': ['analysis_unavailable'], 'requires_reasoning': True, 'estimated_branches': 2, 'reasoning_type': 'tot', 'analysis_reasoning': 'AI analysis unavailable, using fallback assessment'}, 'reasoning_branches': [{'branch_id': 'branch_0', 'perspective': 'notification_component_identification', 'description': 'Identify all notification-related components, classes, and methods within HelloWorldApp to map the system architecture', 'focus_area': 'notification sys